<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Brynner returns two weeks after his first visit. His PET-CT and brain MRI were done eleven days ago, and the endobronchial ultrasound biopsy six days ago. He saw the thoracic oncologist this morning and was told he has adenocarcinoma of the lung that has spread to three bones. His voice is still weak and breathy, and he has not sung since the tour paused. He has a little dry cough in the mornings, no blood in his sputum, and no breathlessness on the level. He has no bone, back, rib, or hip pain, no headache, and no weakness or numbness. His weight is steady. He is sleeping less well with worry, but he says he wants every fact and wants to get back on stage. He has not smoked for 12 years. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Results since last visit</td><td>PET-CT and brain MRI; endobronchial ultrasound biopsy: adenocarcinoma, PD-L1 70 percent; plasma testing without an actionable alteration; tissue sequencing pending</td></tr><tr><td>Voice</td><td>Weak and breathy; not singing</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Morning dry cough; no hemoptysis; no breathlessness on the level</td></tr><tr><td>Bone and neurological symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Coping</td><td>Worried and sleeping less; distress thermometer 6 of 10</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

