    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Adenocarcinoma of the left upper lobe of the lung, stage IVB (cT4 N2 M1c, AJCC 8th edition), unresectable: the primary invades the mediastinum at the aortopulmonary window; bone metastases; PD-L1 tumor proportion score 70 percent (22C3); ECOG performance status 1; comprehensive genomic profiling results in the notes</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C34.12</td><td>S — Synthetic modern histology, stage, and biomarkers linked to his documented inoperable lung cancer of September 1983.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Bone metastases at T10, the right ilium, and the left sixth rib on PET-CT, without pain, fracture, or cord compression</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C79.51</td><td>S — Synthetic metastatic sites chosen so that first-line systemic therapy is the standard of care; no source describes the spread of his cancer.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Left vocal fold paralysis with a breathy, weak voice, most likely from left recurrent laryngeal nerve involvement by disease in the aortopulmonary window</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
