  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adenocarcinoma of the left upper lobe, stage IVB (cT4 N2 M1c) (C34.12)</content>. Tissue diagnosis made: adenocarcinoma, TTF-1 positive, PD-L1 tumor proportion score 70 percent. Staged by PET-CT and brain MRI: mediastinal invasion (T4), aortopulmonary window and subcarinal nodes (N2), and three bone metastases (M1c); no brain metastases. ECOG 1. Plasma testing shows no actionable alteration; tissue sequencing is still pending. The thoracic oncologist recommends first-line pembrolizumab if tissue sequencing confirms no actionable alteration, and not starting an immune checkpoint inhibitor before that result. [S]<list><item>Await tissue sequencing, expected within a week; treatment decision at the next visit.</item><item>Baseline immune-related adverse event laboratory panel before the first infusion.</item><item>Dental examination on Friday, before a bone-modifying agent.</item><item>Palliative care visit in two weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bone metastases, without pain or fracture (C79.51)</content>. Three lytic lesions without pain, fracture, or threatened cord; calcium normal. [S]<list><item>Zoledronic acid every 12 weeks after the dental examination.</item><item>Call at once for new back pain, leg weakness, or numbness.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left vocal fold paralysis (J38.01)</content>. Hoarseness from recurrent laryngeal nerve involvement; recovery is unlikely while the tumor is present, but injection medialization can restore much of his voice. [S]<list><item>Injection medialization by the ENT surgeon in three weeks.</item><item>Voice therapy with a speech-language pathologist.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Former smoker (Z87.891)</content>. No tobacco for 12 years; no cessation treatment needed. [S]<list><item>Confirm abstinence at each visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>PD-L1 immunohistochemistry (tumor proportion score)</td><td>At diagnosis; repeat at progression</td><td>Completed today</td><td>22C3 assay on the endobronchial ultrasound sample: tumor proportion score 70 percent</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Broad molecular profiling (tissue and plasma)</td><td>At diagnosis of advanced nonsquamous NSCLC: EGFR, ALK, ROS1, BRAF, KRAS (including G12C), MET exon 14, RET, NTRK, HER2, NRG1, and PD-L1; repeat at progression</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Plasma cell-free DNA: no actionable alteration. Tissue next-generation sequencing pending; therapy waits for it</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Staging PET-CT and brain MRI</td><td>At diagnosis of suspected advanced disease</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed today: cT4 N2 M1c (bone), no brain metastases</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Immune-related adverse event laboratory panel</td><td>Before each immunotherapy infusion: TSH, liver tests, glucose; cortisol at baseline and as indicated</td><td>Due</td><td>Baseline panel before the first infusion</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Response assessment imaging</td><td>Every 6 to 12 weeks on active systemic therapy</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No systemic therapy started yet</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dyspnea and cough assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Morning dry cough; breathless on two flights of stairs; no hemoptysis</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Smoking status and cessation support</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; no tobacco for 12 years</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Distress and symptom screening (NCCN Distress Thermometer, ESAS)</td><td>Every visit; at minimum at key transitions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Distress thermometer 6 of 10 (worry, work, voice); ESAS total 18</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cancer-related fatigue screening</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tires by evening; ESAS tiredness 4 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression and anxiety screening</td><td>At least yearly; more often during active treatment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 5 two weeks ago; rescreen during treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight and dietary review</td><td>Each follow-up</td><td>Completed today</td><td>72.0 kg, stable; eating normally</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dental evaluation before a bone-modifying agent</td><td>Baseline, then periodically on zoledronic acid or denosumab</td><td>Due</td><td>Dental examination booked for Friday</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Chemotherapy-induced peripheral neuropathy</td><td>Every visit during and after platinum or taxane</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No platinum or taxane planned</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Thoracic oncology consultation</td><td>At diagnosis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; stage IVB confirmed; pembrolizumab planned if tissue sequencing shows no actionable alteration</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Early integrated palliative care</td><td>Within eight weeks of diagnosis of advanced cancer</td><td>Referred</td><td>First visit in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At diagnosis and at changes in health</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First conversation today: he wants full information and full treatment, and to return to the stage</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Voice and work support</td><td>As needed</td><td>Referred</td><td>Injection medialization and voice therapy arranged</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Immunizations per ACIP</td><td>Yearly review</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, and RSV to be reviewed at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Pulmonary rehabilitation</td><td>Before and after lung resection, or for symptomatic dyspnea or deconditioning</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No resection; not deconditioned</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Tissue diagnosis, full staging, PD-L1, and comprehensive biomarker results before any systemic therapy, within three weeks of presentation. In progress; target 2026-09-22 [S]</item><item>First palliative care visit within eight weeks of diagnosis. In progress; target 2026-10-13 [S]</item><item>A voice strong enough for rehearsal by the second cycle. In progress; target 2026-10-13 [S]</item><item>No grade 2 or higher immune-related adverse event missed: laboratory panel before each infusion and symptom review at each visit. In progress; target 2026-10-13 [S]</item><item>Zoledronic acid started only after a dental examination and normal calcium and kidney function. In progress; target 2026-10-13 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, lung cancer monograph (2026); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (2026); Management of Immune-Related Adverse Events in Patients Treated With Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy: ASCO Guideline Update (2021); Integration of Palliative Care Into Standard Oncology Care: American Society of Clinical Oncology Clinical Practice Guideline Update (2017); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Distress Management (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Dental examination on Friday. Visit next week for the tissue sequencing result and the treatment start. Palliative care in two weeks. Voice injection in three weeks. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-22: biomarker results and start of first-line pembrolizumab. [S]</paragraph></text>

